  "title": "Election Commission Clarifies Form 6 for Re-enrolment",
  "summary": "The Election Commission (EC) clarified that electors whose names do not appear in the draft electoral roll must seek inclusion afresh under the Special Intensive Revision (SIR) or afterwards, regardless of whether they had been enrolled previously. The EC also stated that previously enrolled voters can submit Form 6 for inclusion if their names are missing from the draft SIR rolls, as long as they provide a declaration that their name is being included in the electoral list for the first time.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The ECI clarified that electors whose names do not appear in the draft roll must seek inclusion afresh under the SIR or afterwards.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The EC also stated that previously enrolled voters can submit Form 6 for inclusion if their names are missing from the draft SIR rolls.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
