    {
      "title": "Previously enrolled voters can file Form 6 if missing from SIR rolls: EC",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/previously-enrolled-voters-can-file-form-6-if-missing-from-sir-rolls-ec-126110301817_1.html",
      "description": "The Election Commission on Tuesday said previously enrolled voters can submit Form 6 for inclusion as electors if their names are missing from draft Special Intensive Revision (SIR) rolls.\nThe clarification comes amid concerns among those whose names have been deleted from draft SIR rolls that submitting Form 6, which carries a declaration that the applicant is seeking inclusion in the voters' list for the first time, could amount to making a false declaration and invite prosecution under the Representation of the People Act.\nIn a letter to all state chief electoral officers, the Election Commission (EC) said that it has been brought to its notice that certain people whose names do not figure in the draft electoral roll published during the ongoing SIR are hesitant to submit Form 6 as they are also required to furnish a declaration prescribed in the form to the effect that their name is being included in the electoral rolls for the first time.\n\"Therefore, such electors believe that",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-03T15:21:47"
    }
